# Docker build-context excludes for the stock-desk backend image.
#
# ADR-0012 C-52 governs why this file exists at all: the sector-momentum
# *judgement* (NE-7's ci_passed_commit check) never runs inside this image --
# it only runs on a host git checkout (Options K1). This image is still used
# to serve the read-only API and, per compose.yaml, to run the scheduler
# process for everything else (data refresh, alerts, PIT snapshot capture);
# it is simply never the process that is allowed to *judge* the sector card.
# Excluding tests/ below does not change that conclusion -- NE-7 already
# fails closed inside any image because `.git` is absent (C-52), independent
# of whether the test files happen to be present.
#
# Dockerfile only `COPY`s pyproject.toml, uv.lock and app/, so none of this
# is actually copied into the image layers today; this file matters anyway
# because .dockerignore controls what gets uploaded into the *build context*
# sent to the Docker daemon, not just what a COPY instruction picks up -- a
# broadened COPY (e.g. an accidental `COPY . .` in a future edit) must not be
# able to smuggle any of this in either.

# --- Secrets (never in the image, never even in the build context) ---
# ADR-0012 C-52 explicit requirement.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
# Local OpenAI Codex CLI state/session data (company-wide convention, see
# root .gitignore); may contain local session artifacts, never a build input.
.codex/

# --- Local NE-7 build attestation (ADR-0012 C-36, C-52) ---
# app/_build/ci_attestation.json is meaningful only bound to the exact git
# commit and worktree state it was produced on (scripts/attest_sector_gate.py
# on the host checkout). Baking a stale copy into an image would be
# misleading even though app.services.sector_attestation.verify() already
# fails closed on a missing `.git` regardless (defense in depth, not the
# primary control).
app/_build/

# --- Host virtual environment ---
# The image builds its own venv via `uv sync --frozen` against uv.lock
# inside the container; a host .venv/ is a different platform/arch (this
# repo is developed and CI'd on Linux, but the operator's own workstation
# may be Windows) and is large enough to slow every build context upload.
.venv/

# --- Bytecode and tool caches ---
# Never needed at runtime; regenerated on first import. Keeping them out
# also avoids ever shipping stale .pyc files that no longer match app/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Local SQLite data files ---
# The three ADR-0012 databases (main / market / research) and any dev/demo
# DB must never be baked into an image: they hold real position data and,
# per D-2, the market DB is an append-only PIT artifact that must not be
# silently duplicated into an unrelated build. Runtime data always comes
# from a mounted path (STOCK_DESK_DB_PATH / STOCK_DESK_MARKET_DB_PATH /
# STOCK_DESK_RESEARCH_DB_PATH), never from the image.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
/data/

# --- Tests ---
# Not needed to run the API or scheduler process; excluding them shrinks the
# image and build context. Per the note above, this is a hygiene move only:
# it does not change C-52's conclusion, since the image already cannot judge
# (no `.git`) with or without tests/ present.
tests/
